{"schema_version":"1.0.0","metadata":{"trial_id":"202610080722-shophouse-contract","prompting_method_id":"concept-build-free.v0","model_id":"claude-opus-5-5","seed":11,"server_state_id":"concept-free.v1"},"style":{"name":"Shophouse: The Redstone Exchange — timber-framed craftsman's shophouse over limewashed stall bays","rationale":"Dark oak posts sit directly over the white concrete stall walls (x 0,4,8,11), so the ground and upper rhythms share columns. A stripped-spruce bressummer at y5 carries three lit redstone lamps over the stall centres as the shop sign. Above it are an upside-down spruce-stair sill row and glazed bays at y7-8, under a continuous wall plate at y9. The only street projection is the y10 spruce-stair eave at z=-1. The roof is side-gabled at half pitch (stair/top-slab courses) with a stripped-spruce ridge beam at y12 under a slab ridge at y13. The flush gables use plank verges, a tie beam, a king post, and twin pane vents. There is a small gable dormer at x5-7 with a centre pane, and a brick chimney at x2 z9 capped by a lit campfire. Sills face outward (half=top, back to the wall) so their lip reads as a corbel without leaving the plane. To keep the back door inside the lot, the upper storey steps back to z=9 over x9-11. This makes a roofed porch where a quarter-turn spruce stair climbs y1 to y5 to the door. A hanging lantern on a chain and azalea greenery give the porch life. The back-left yard became a post-supported undercroft under the jettied upper floor, with barrels, a composter, potted plants, and a hanging lantern. Every street-facing front cell y5-9 is solid or glass. Nothing is placed in R, H, stall-front, or W/B cells, and nothing sits outside the lot below y10."},"palette":{"manifest":["minecraft:spruce_planks","minecraft:oak_planks","minecraft:stripped_spruce_log","minecraft:dark_oak_log","minecraft:redstone_lamp","minecraft:glass_pane","minecraft:spruce_stairs","minecraft:spruce_slab","minecraft:spruce_door","minecraft:bricks","min